    "math_academy_id": "q-89877",
    "knowledge_point_id": "3f28fbcc-6d9c-5dc7-89cc-13255db78765",
    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Second Derivative at a Point on a Solution Curve",
    "problem": "The function $y=f(x)$ satisfies the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y+{e}^{x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven that the point $P(-1,0)$ lies on the graph of the function, evaluate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}$ at $P.$",
    "worked_solution": "To find an expression for the second derivative, we differentiate the equation with respect to $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the given expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ into the above and simplify the resulting expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =(y+{e}^{x})+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =y+2{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the coordinates of our point into the above expression for the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}|}_{(-1,0)} & ={(y+2{e}^{x})|}_{(-1,0)} \\\\  & =0+2{e}^{-1} \\\\  & =2{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
