    "reasoning": "All 16 captured worked solutions give mathematically correct answers. For q-7973 and q-7975, standard form gives asymptote slopes b/a=5/2 and 5/4. For q-50974, the quadratic Taylor coefficient is f''(-2)/2, so f''(-2)=32. For q-81064, the graph at x=-1 has positive height, positive slope, and negative concavity, matching option 4. For q-89877, differentiating gives y''=y'+e^x=y+2e^x, hence 2e^{-1}. For q-65399, factoring and using sec²x−tan²x=1 gives sec²x+tan²x. For q-65410, the denominator factors as sec(alpha)(sec(alpha)+1), giving cos(alpha) on the original expression's domain. For q-89197 and q-106528, sec²t−tan²t=1 gives the stated parameterization and Cartesian equation. For q-89350, positive secant on (-pi/2,pi/2) traces the right branch. For q-15479 and q-126359, the cubic Taylor coefficients are 24/3!=4 and 6/3!=1. For q-123765, t≤0 gives exactly x≥1. For q-73602, elimination gives y=2−(x+1)²/4, with −7≤x≤5, vertex (-1,2), and endpoints (-7,-7),(5,-7); option 1 is the corresponding downward-parabola depiction, while the worked-solution image explicitly marks the bounded curve. For q-123785, x+y=2 with −4≤x≤5 gives the segment from (5,-3) to (-4,6), matching option 4; the source image adds sampled points. For q-125968, the geometric ratio is −2/e with magnitude less than 1, giving sum e/(e+2). The graph answers use different image files from their worked solutions but depict the corresponding curves. No earlier submitted answers or grades were supplied; confirmation rests on each question's own captured worked solution.",
